<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eight Banners</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1601</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Banner forces, bannermen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Eight Banners were the military and administrative organisation created by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchus">Manchu</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nurhaci">Nurhaci</a> around 1601. All Manchu households were enrolled in banners, later joined by Mongol and Han banners. They formed the core of the force that conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and remained a privileged hereditary military <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caste">caste</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eight-banners.jpg" alt="Eight Banners" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giuseppe Castiglione · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E4%B9%BE%E9%9A%86%E5%A4%A7%E9%98%85%E5%9B%BE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
